{
  "name": "mayfly",
  "_about": "A mayfly -- the green drake (Ephemera danica), 2 cm long with three tails half as long again: a dainty, short-lived fly of rivers; big dark eyes, tiny bristle antennae; the wings held upright together over the back like a sail -- the forewing a big veined triangle, cream-tinted with dark spots, the hindwing small; a slender cream abdomen curving up, dark-marked toward its end, with three long tails; the long forelegs held forward. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
